Hey Andrew,
Thanks for your reply on the below.
Reviewing both connectors, it appears they are behaving differently.
For connector 1, we see EVSuspended after going into charging and apply voltage.
While for connector 3, it also goes into charging and applying voltage, but then appears to receive a “remotestop” from the OCPP backend.
I’m not sure if this is some pre-defined logic which otherwise has been working?
